@startuml
title 3.3.5 Create a LOST post
caption UC-018 | Implemented
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: apps/api-node/src/modules/posts/application/post.use-cases.ts
' Main entity migration: apps/api-node/src/migrations/002_lost_found_schema.sql
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "User" as Actor
participant "Post Form" as Page
participant "Posts API" as API
participant "Post Service" as Service
participant "posts" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Create a LOST post
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/posts (type=LOST)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Create a LOST post
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Validate incident time, leaf category and location relationships
Service -> Service: 6: Normalize title and description; use authenticated owner ID
Service -> Service: 7: Begin transaction; lock related business context
Service -> Table: 8: INSERT LOST post with expiry and visibility
activate Table
Table --> Service: 9: Write result inside transaction
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 10: Persist supplied analysis tags as support signals
Service -> Service: 11: Commit atomically; propagate errors, never fabricate success
Service -> Service: 12: Run matching best effort after commit; keep valid post on failure
Service --> API: 13: Created LOST post
API --> Page: 14: HTTP 201: Created LOST post
Page --> Actor: 15: Upload selected images; navigate to matching results
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Image analysis is optional and user-reviewed. Media uploads are separate requests, not part
of the post INSERT.
endlegend
@enduml
